{:edb/db-before-t 1883 :edb/db-after-t 1884 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535196 50 #inst "2026-10-08T19:18:29.079Z" 13194139535196 true] [17592186184277 1020 #edb/ref 17592186336847 13194139535196 true] [17592186184277 1020 #edb/ref 17592186336861 13194139535196 true] [17592186184278 1020 #edb/ref 17592186336854 13194139535196 true] [17592186184279 1020 #edb/ref 17592186336869 13194139535196 true] [17592186184684 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535196 true] [17592186184684 1100 "Find the solution of $x^{2} \\ge 5x + 6$." 13194139535196 false] [17592186184684 1100 "Find the solution of ${x}^{2}\\ge 5x+6.$" 13194139535196 true] [17592186184684 1145 "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the numbers to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & \\ge 5x+6 \\\\ {x}^{2}-5x-6 & \\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y={x}^{2}-5x-6$ lies above the $x$-axis or touches this axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-5x-6 & =0 \\\\ (x+1)(x-6) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=-1$ and $x=6,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/assets/51c7484f806696105dd570684f8b194d3c1b7fc3ea27d85a1a17f53e6f7d0a64.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-5x-6\\ge 0,\n$$\n\nwe look for the part of the parabola that is above the $x$-axis or touches this axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $x\\le -1$ or $x\\ge 6.$ \n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in (-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [6,\\infty ).$" 13194139535196 true] [17592186336847 1017 #edb/ref 17592186336848 13194139535196 true] [17592186336847 1089 "q-142314" 13194139535196 true] [17592186336847 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535196 true] [17592186336847 1100 "Find the solution of ${x}^{2}+x-12\\le 0.$" 13194139535196 true] [17592186336847 1113 #uuid "fb1e01eb-14f1-577c-a4b7-0a54f287effc" 13194139535196 true] [17592186336847 1145 "To solve the inequality \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+x-12\\le 0,\n$$\n\nwe need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny={x}^{2}+x-12\n$$\n\nlies *below* the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nFirst, let's find the roots of the parabola:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+x-12 & =0 \\\\ (x+4)(x-3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the roots are $x=-4$ and $x=3,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/assets/eda4704129b905a10e379254dfd6d1ff07d593d7f97bbc6126e9d27bfec2f9f2.png)\n\nThe values marked in blue show all $x$-values where the parabola lies *below* the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $-4\\le x\\le 3.$" 13194139535196 true] [17592186336848 1000 #edb/ref 17592186336849 13194139535196 true] [17592186336848 1000 #edb/ref 17592186336850 13194139535196 true] [17592186336848 1000 #edb/ref 17592186336851 13194139535196 true] [17592186336848 1000 #edb/ref 17592186336852 13194139535196 true] [17592186336848 1000 #edb/ref 17592186336853 13194139535196 true] [17592186336848 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535196 true] [17592186336848 1041 "selection" 13194139535196 true] [17592186336848 1104 #edb/ref 17592186336851 13194139535196 true] [17592186336848 1110 #uuid "a1d486a9-0c77-56cb-a5d9-cb60b5077939" 13194139535196 true] [17592186336849 1034 "$x\\le -3$ or $x\\ge 4$" 13194139535196 true] [17592186336849 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535196 true] [17592186336849 1111 #uuid "9aa83bc8-7a74-540d-88db-e19eaa52bbbd" 13194139535196 true] [17592186336850 1034 "-2<x<3" 13194139535196 true] [17592186336850 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535196 true] [17592186336850 1111 #uuid "5123fc09-d68f-5a66-9cb5-ab5d772b00a8" 13194139535196 true] [17592186336851 1034 "-4\\le x\\le 3" 13194139535196 true] [17592186336851 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535196 true] [17592186336851 1111 #uuid "6cc53cb3-ac2c-5c40-b16b-a2c433f70813" 13194139535196 true] [17592186336852 1034 "$x\\le -6$ or $x\\ge 2$" 13194139535196 true] [17592186336852 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535196 true] [17592186336852 1111 #uuid "9df67623-03d3-57a8-b0d0-37e2b6c1bff5" 13194139535196 true] [17592186336853 1034 "-3\\le x\\le 4" 13194139535196 true] [17592186336853 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535196 true] [17592186336853 1111 #uuid "a5e32ab7-f1fa-5556-9c14-764d7b51e7da" 13194139535196 true] [17592186336854 1017 #edb/ref 17592186336855 13194139535196 true] [17592186336854 1017 #edb/ref 17592186336857 13194139535196 true] [17592186336854 1017 #edb/ref 17592186336859 13194139535196 true] [17592186336854 1089 "q-276404" 13194139535196 true] [17592186336854 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535196 true] [17592186336854 1100 "Solve the inequality $6{x}^{2}+21x\\ge 12$ and express the solution set in interval notation.\n\n$x\\in (${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$]\\,⋃\\,[${{field-3}}$,\\,\\infty )$" 13194139535196 true] [17592186336854 1113 #uuid "021dad23-6108-5419-9f6e-96c817c309f7" 13194139535196 true] [17592186336854 1145 "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the terms to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{2}+21x & \\ge 12 \\\\ 6{x}^{2}+21x-12 & \\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y=6{x}^{2}+21x-12$ lies **above** the $x$-axis or touches this axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{2}+21x-12 & =0 \\\\ (6{x}^{2}-3x)+(24x-12) & =0 \\\\ 3x(2x-1)+12(2x-1) & =0 \\\\ (3x+12)(2x-1) & =0 \\\\ 3(x+4)(2x-1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=-4$ and $x=\\frac{1}{2},$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/assets/38c1897ec93625527b48ec689fbd65e9a63056e033fa6a7a0c72473f1188e7ea.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n6{x}^{2}+21x-12\\ge 0,\n$$\n\n \n\nwe look for the part of the parabola that is **above** the $x$-axis or touches this axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $x\\le -4$ or $x\\ge \\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in (-\\infty ,-4]⋃[\\frac{1}{2},\\infty ).$" 13194139535196 true] [17592186336855 1000 #edb/ref 17592186336856 13194139535196 true] [17592186336855 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535196 true] [17592186336855 1041 "field-1" 13194139535196 true] [17592186336855 1104 #edb/ref 17592186336856 13194139535196 true] [17592186336855 1110 #uuid "b7196d3d-50f2-5a3e-855d-aedbdfff5577" 13194139535196 true] [17592186336856 1034 "-\\infty" 13194139535196 true] [17592186336856 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535196 true] [17592186336856 1111 #uuid "e69649ce-42f9-5691-923a-d247fdd42a5a" 13194139535196 true] [17592186336857 1000 #edb/ref 17592186336858 13194139535196 true] [17592186336857 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535196 true] [17592186336857 1041 "field-2" 13194139535196 true] [17592186336857 1104 #edb/ref 17592186336858 13194139535196 true] [17592186336857 1110 #uuid "0486b523-ad57-5ead-824b-4856aee7f54b" 13194139535196 true] [17592186336858 1034 "-4" 13194139535196 true] [17592186336858 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535196 true] [17592186336858 1111 #uuid "f93f7865-bb56-5650-a8e1-210b3358e2a4" 13194139535196 true] [17592186336859 1000 #edb/ref 17592186336860 13194139535196 true] [17592186336859 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535196 true] [17592186336859 1041 "field-3" 13194139535196 true] [17592186336859 1104 #edb/ref 17592186336860 13194139535196 true] [17592186336859 1110 #uuid "52611d45-624a-5dbc-bf7a-21bde6074b0e" 13194139535196 true] [17592186336860 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139535196 true] [17592186336860 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535196 true] [17592186336860 1111 #uuid "919706fc-