e so that the right-hand side is $0.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}-17x & >-2{x}^{2}+45 \\\\ 6{x}^{2}-17x-45 & >0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y=6{x}^{2}-17x-45$ lies **above** the $x$-axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{2}-17x-45 & =0 \\\\ (6{x}^{2}-27x)+(10x-45) & =0 \\\\ 3x(2x-9)+5(2x-9) & =0 \\\\ (3x+5)(2x-9) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=-\\frac{5}{3}$ and $x=\\frac{9}{2},$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/assets/f73c9906e6b65d1ddbda91619c7ffbb77408faa0541e2bc16565e0127d334312.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n6{x}^{2}-17x-45>0,\n$$\n\n \nwe look for the part of the parabola that is **above** the $x$-axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $x<-\\frac{5}{3}$ or $x>\\frac{9}{2}.$\n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in (-\\infty ,-\\frac{5}{3})⋃(\\frac{9}{2},\\infty ).$" 13194139535196 true] [17592186336870 1000 #edb/ref 17592186336871 13194139535196 true] [17592186336870 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535196 true] [17592186336870 1041 "field-1" 13194139535196 true] [17592186336870 1104 #edb/ref 17592186336871 13194139535196 true] [17592186336870 1110 #uuid "bfdf0d4c-944a-5cf5-881e-dcbc6b721475" 13194139535196 true] [17592186336871 1034 "-\\infty" 13194139535196 true] [17592186336871 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535196 true] [17592186336871 1111 #uuid "efac5182-d12a-5b78-968c-f9aa01f5d7fb" 13194139535196 true] [17592186336872 1000 #edb/ref 17592186336873 13194139535196 true] [17592186336872 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535196 true] [17592186336872 1041 "field-2" 13194139535196 true] [17592186336872 1104 #edb/ref 17592186336873 13194139535196 true] [17592186336872 1110 #uuid "b868b0e9-7ae0-50f6-8243-7053e9a125f2" 13194139535196 true] [17592186336873 1034 "-\\frac{5}{3}" 13194139535196 tr